===Etymology===
1890, {{bor|en|de|Wurst||sausage, wurst|withtext=1}} from {{der|en|gmh|wurst}}, from {{der|en|goh|wurst}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*wurstiz||something turned or twisted}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*wert-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*werd-||to turn}}. Akin to {{cog|osx|worst||wurst}}, {{cog|ang|weorþan||to turn, become}}. Unrelated to {{m|en|worsted||type of yarn}}. More at {{m|en|worth||to be, become, betide}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|GA}} {{IPA|/wɝst/|/vɝst/|/vʊɹst/|lang=en}}
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|/wɜːst/|/vɜːst/|/vʊəst/|lang=en}}
* {{homophones|worst|lang=en}} {{qualifier|one pronunciation}}
* {{rhymes|ɜː(ɹ)st|lang=en}}

